  "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y={log}_{6}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14245974/assets/d8d3f9dc995d8801d451b15129860362efa772178cdc3ef07be5adb6a1da5c45.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has a zero at $x=1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. As $x$ increases, $y$ increases without bound. Therefore, $y\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty $\n\n- Statement III is true.\n\nIn conclusion, only statement III is true.",
